# Own-wording text for the Kobold Press Compilation spells (Open5e, OGL 1.0a). Class lists come from the source (Open5e v1 dnd_class).
TEXT = {
"Curse of Formlessness": ["Level 6. Touch: Con save or cursed with an amorphous body. Resist slashing and piercing, ignore crit damage, but no items, no spells, half speed, no winged flight, disadvantage on Dex checks and saves while burdened. The target can repeat the save as an action to shake it for a turn.",
 "A creature you touch makes a Constitution save or is cursed with a shifting, shapeless body. Spells that change shape (polymorph) do not end the curse but hold the creature in a stable form until they end, as do shapechange and stoneskin. While cursed, the target resists slashing and piercing damage and ignores the extra damage of critical hits, but cannot hold or use items, cast spells or activate magic items. Its movement is halved and winged flight is impossible. Armor, clothing, helmets and rings become useless. Large carried or worn items such as armor, backpacks or clothes hinder it, giving disadvantage on Dexterity checks and saves while in place. The afflicted creature can use its action to repeat the save, and on a success it ignores the penalties until the start of its next turn."],
"Doom of Voracity": ["Level 3. A 10 ft radius, 10 ft deep extradimensional pit within 120 ft that grows. Dex save to avoid falling in. When it ends, creatures inside make a Con save or are stunned for 2 rounds.",
 "A ripple of dark energy opens a 10 ft radius, 10 ft deep extradimensional pit on a horizontal surface big enough to hold it. It has no weight and does not displace the underlying material. Any creature standing on the original space, or on a space as the pit grows, makes a Dexterity save to avoid falling in. The sloped edges crumble constantly, and a creature next to the pit when it expands makes a Dexterity save to avoid falling. The source text is damaged in the middle of the description, so the growth and fall rules should be checked in the book. When the spell ends, creatures in the pit make a Constitution save. Those who succeed rise with the bottom of the pit to the original surface. Those who fail also rise but are stunned for 2 rounds. Higher slots: pit depth +10 ft per slot level above 3rd."],
"Hirvsth's Call": ["Level 4. A spectral pony herd drags a Large or smaller creature 60 ft each round. Dex save to avoid. The target is prone, restrained, takes 1d6 bludgeoning per 20 ft, and can escape with a Str or Dex check against your spell DC.",
 "You summon a spectral herd of ponies to haul off a creature you see in range, no bigger than Large. It makes a Dexterity save and on a success nothing happens. On a failure a spectral rope wraps around it and pulls it 60 ft in a direction you choose as the herd races away. The ponies keep running that way for the duration, steering around impassable obstacles. You cannot change the direction once chosen. The ponies ignore difficult terrain and are immune to damage. The target is prone and immobilized but can use its action for a Strength or Dexterity check against your spell DC to escape. It takes 1d6 bludgeoning for every 20 ft it is dragged. The herd moves 60 ft each round at the start of your turn. Higher slots: one more target per slot level above 4th."],
"Lesser Ley Protection": ["Level 5. A 10 ft cube of antimagic against ley line magic up to level 5. Ley spells have no effect on creatures in it, and active ley effects on them are suppressed. You can exclude individuals.",
 "You create a 10 ft cube in range that shields against ley line magic. Ley line spells and effects up to level 5 that target a creature in the cube have no effect on it. Active ley line spells and effects up to level 5 on a creature or object inside are suppressed while it stays there. The area of such a spell or effect cannot extend into the cube, and where it overlaps (such as lesser ley pulse) the covered part is suppressed. The cube does nothing against other magic. You can exclude specific individuals from the protection. Higher slots: at slot 7 or higher the duration is concentration, up to 1 hour."],
"Ley Disturbance": ["Level 3. In your bound forest for 1 hour, sense any ley line manipulation or ley spellcasting within 5 miles, with approximate direction and distance but not exact location.",
 "While in your bound forest you tune your senses to disturbances in its ley energy. For the duration you know of any ley line manipulation or ley spellcasting within 5 miles, along with the approximate distance and general direction to each. You do not learn the exact location, and it does not find the ley lines themselves, only their use or change."],
"Locate Red Portal": ["Level 3. 10 minutes. Sense dimensional portals within 60 ft and whether they are one- or two-way. An action lets you peek at the other end. DC 25 Intelligence check for an unknown destination.",
 "For the duration you sense any dimensional portals within range and whether each is one-way or two-way. When you sense one, you can use your action to peer through it and glimpse the area at the other end of the shadow road. If you have never visited the destination you can make a DC 25 Intelligence check (Arcana, History or Nature, whichever fits best) to work out where and when it leads."],
"Morphic Flux": ["Level 7. Your body churns for 1 minute: resist slashing and piercing, ignore crit extra damage, squeeze through Tiny spaces, and once per round as a bonus action make an unarmed attack with a new limb that deals the type you choose.",
 "Your body becomes highly mutable. Flesh shifts and quivers, sprouting limbs and eyes only to reabsorb them. For the duration you resist slashing and piercing damage and ignore the extra damage of critical hits. You can squeeze through Tiny spaces without penalty. Once per round as a bonus action you can make an unarmed attack with a newly grown limb, treated as a normal unarmed attack, and you choose whether it deals bludgeoning, piercing or slashing."],
"Open Red Portal": ["Level 9. Needs a titanic or strong ley line. Open a two-way Red Portal on the shadow road to a precise place on any plane, now or up to 1,000 years back on the Material Plane. Lasts 10 minutes. Deities can block it.",
 "You tap a titanic or strong ley line (see the Ley Initiate feat) and open a new two-way Red Portal on the shadow road, leading to a precise location you choose on any plane. On the Prime Material Plane the destination can be in the present or up to 1,000 years in the past. The portal lasts for the duration. Deities and other planar rulers can prevent portals opening in their presence or domains."],
"Perun's Doom": ["Level 3. A vortex in a 20 ft radius cylinder within 60 ft. Str save: 3d8 bludgeoning, pulled to the center and thrown 50 ft up. Hitting a ceiling deals falling damage for the unspent height.",
 "A strong wind swirls from your hand to a point in range and explodes into a vortex. Each creature in a 20 ft radius cylinder there makes a Strength save. On a failure it takes 3d8 bludgeoning, is pulled to the center and thrown 50 ft into the air. If it strikes a solid obstruction such as a ceiling, it takes bludgeoning damage as if it fell (50 ft minus the distance it rose), for example 40 ft or 4d6 after rising only 10 ft. Higher slots: +10 ft of lift per slot level above 3rd."],
"Reset Red Portal": ["Level 5. Reset the destination of a Red Portal within 10 ft for 1 hour to a place you name in the present day. After it ends, it returns to the original (50%) or a random new destination.",
 "You reset the destination of a Red Portal in range, diverting the shadow road to a location of your choice in the present day. You can name it in general terms (a city, a ruler's home, a hall) and anyone stepping through while the spell lasts arrives in or near it, as the GM decides. When the spell ends the portal returns to its original destination (50% chance) or to a new random one from the Destinations table. Higher slots: you can name a destination up to 100 years in the past for each slot level above 5th."],
"Sanguine Spear": ["Level 2. Touch the blood of a corpse dead less than 24 hours to make a frozen blood spear: a +1 spear that deals cold. It melts if away from your hand for over a round. Slot 4: +2, slot 6: +3.",
 "You draw blood from a creature dead no longer than 24 hours and shape it into a spear of frozen blood. It works as a +1 spear that deals cold damage instead of piercing. If it leaves your hand for more than 1 round it melts and the spell ends. Higher slots: a 4th-level slot makes a +2 spear and a 6th-level slot a +3 spear."],
"Seal Red Portal": ["Level 6. Seal a Red Portal or other dimensional gate within 60 ft until dispelled. A sealed portal cannot be found with locate Red Portal.",
 "You seal a Red Portal or other dimensional gate in range, making it inoperable until the spell is dispelled. While sealed it cannot be found with the locate Red Portal spell."],
"Selfish Wish": ["Level 9. Like wish, but the GM twists it, with drawbacks. It needs a pint of the wisher's blood. For 2 minutes you gain double speed, an extra action each round, and +3 AC.",
 "A selfish wish grants a supplicant's desire in exchange for power. It alters reality like wish but the result is usually twisted or misread, and the GM must pervert every casting. Careful wording may soften the harm, but drawbacks always occur. The wish-maker supplies a pint of blood and states the desire. It can produce any effect wish can, and effects beyond that bring worse drawbacks (for example, a huge Strength gain with an equal Intelligence loss). In exchange the caster gets power for 2 minutes: doubled speed, one extra action each round as with haste, and +3 to Armor Class."],
"Shadow Spawn": ["Level 6. Casting 4 hours. Consume a corpse and raise a shadowy duplicate as a shadow beast with dim memories and free will.",
 "Casting this spell consumes the corpse of a creature and makes a shadowy duplicate. The creature returns as a shadow beast. It has dim memories of its former life and keeps free will, so the caster should be ready to make an attractive offer to win its cooperation."],
"Stigmata of the Red Goddess": ["Level 2. Bleed as tribute for 3 rounds: take 1 piercing damage at the start of each turn and gain +2 damage on rolls. Any healing ends it. Higher slots raise both and the duration.",
 "You cut yourself and bleed as tribute to Marena, gaining power while the blood flows. It usually shows as blood from the eyes or ears, or wounds on the neck or chest. You take 1 piercing damage at the start of each turn and gain a +2 bonus on damage rolls. Any healing you receive, magical or not, ends the spell. Higher slots: the damage you take and the bonus each rise by 1 per slot level above 2nd, and the duration rises by 1 round per slot level above 2nd."],
"The Black God's Blessing": ["Level 9. Casting 7 hours. A DC 20 spellcasting check to demand Chernobog's power for a touched target: success grants darkvision 60 ft and cold immunity, failure makes caster and target permanently fire-vulnerable (until remove curse).",
 "After contacting the Black God, the ritual caster demands that Chernobog deposit part of his power into the target creature. For him to comply, the caster must succeed on a DC 20 spellcasting check. If the check fails, the spell fails and the caster and the target become permanently vulnerable to fire, which remove curse or comparable magic can end. If it succeeds, the target gains darkvision (60 ft) and immunity to cold. Chernobog can revoke the gifts if the recipient's devotion wavers."],
}
